    "body": "Protected-source edits could bypass the path-filtered release workflow. This adds three independent always-on jobs for canonical frozen-source preservation, exact isolated TeX regeneration and actual historical restoration in a Linux network namespace.\n\n## Resulting behavior\n- Preserve 340 historical entries plus all 29 accepted release files. Compare independently hashed canonical Git objects, modes and closed-root topology while allowing additive research and later release versions.\n- Render the pinned accepted builder/helper with the original research SHA in `python -I -S -B`; compare all 71,379 TeX bytes independently of preservation.\n- Deliver a supplement with 36 refs, 26 input commits and 8,202 reachable objects, original R C10 ZIP, complete review/page relationships and all final workflow/job/log captures.\n- Import an empty object database, run strict object checks, validate exact parents/trees/ancestry, replay the unchanged release/package verifiers and 29 legacy tests, and recheck original R C10 content.\n\n## Codex review fixes\nRequired contexts expose no dispatch trigger and their context CLI rejects dispatch. Workflow validation fixes effective read-only permissions/direct commands and pins the complete reviewed profile, covering backgrounding, extra actions/steps, event filters and runtime drift. Review submissions and threads crossbind to original captured pages, exhaustive inline comments, review IDs and mandatory timestamps. Every job needs its own exact endpoint and valid timestamped UTF-8 log; an unopened run ZIP cannot substitute.\n\nIndependent repaired-hash probes verified the intended semantic failures after both inventory layers passed. PRES-23 also covers 12 add/edit/delete mutations across both Lean trees and root files, including unprotected deletions that pass permanent preservation and fail the separate one-time scope check.\n\n## Exact source and archive\nCurrent head: `cc114ee60ff8749b3bb64bb24a8d5e76d2120af9`. Fresh CI is running; previous heads' green results are historical evidence only. The subsequent base refresh after #78 will require another genuine H/B/S execution.\n\nAccepted reference: `d8a4ffb5b63eb9359a4c0af9134b4f9a3c529618`.\nTooling snapshot: `a83d57a707afc91861fc5fec853d01f576ba0334`.\nBundle SHA-256: `56c401a24130fd37231d667fdbad3f5578587bb6a1c6d3c406698bd5a966537f`.\nSupplement manifest SHA-256: `019f816a67d492e65dfb3c3873d2f8a353b08b7706a73489251190a42572710a`.\nPublication candidate: 68 entries / 7,437,026 bytes; SHA-256 `da51255e8f47c3c3e16ef28fd41611eb532f370887722654dc88e01ac7dd97d1`.\n\nNo Lean/root, release, application-schema or pinned dependency changes; zero theorem declarations or scientific promotions. The 108-case registry contains 87 unit, two integration, six live-PR, one review and 12 rollout requirements; method counts are reported separately, never treated as 108 completed cases.\n\n## Deferred operations\nReviewer and publication destination remain undetermined at the user's request. The ruleset is disabled. Settings activation/read-back, remote archival tag and external publication remain OPEN. The Git ZIP is a publication candidate, not a completed external rollout. Candidate-owned checker code still requires independent review; hashes do not create publisher authentication.\n\nSee `docs/V020_HARDENING.md` and `archival/v0.2.0/README.md` for execution and trust boundaries.",
